---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro"
import PageFooter from "../components/PageFooter.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Packstack" description="Privacy Policy for Packstack: what we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and the choices you have.">
  <div class="bg-background min-h-screen">
    <PageHeader />

    <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-12 prose prose-invert prose-sm">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-label text-sm mt-0 mb-10">Effective Date: October 9, 2026</p>

      <p>
        Packstack, LLC ("Packstack," "we," "us," or "our") operates the website
        <a href="https://www.packstack.io">www.packstack.io</a>, the web application at
        <a href="https://app.packstack.io">app.packstack.io</a>, and the Packstack mobile apps
        for iOS and Android (collectively, the "Service"). This Privacy Policy explains what
        information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and the choices you have.
      </p>

      <p>
        By using the Service, you agree to this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please do not
        use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>Account Information</h3>
      <p>
        You can sign in with a one-time code sent to your email address, or with Google or Apple.
        We collect your <strong>email address</strong>. If you sign in with Google or Apple, we
        also receive the <strong>name</strong> you have on that account (Apple may give us a
        private relay email address instead of your real one). We do not receive or store your
        Google or Apple password.
      </p>

      <h3>Profile Information (optional)</h3>
      <p>
        You can add a username, display name, bio, profile photo, and links to your social media
        profiles. This information appears on your public profile.
      </p>

      <h3>Hiker Profile (optional)</h3>
      <p>
        To calculate calorie, food, and water estimates, you can enter your <strong>body weight,
        height, year of birth, sex, and body type</strong>. We use this information only to
        calculate those estimates for you. We do not make it public, use it for advertising, or
        send it to the AI providers described below.
      </p>

      <h3>Content You Create</h3>
      <p>
        We store the gear in your gear closet (including weights, prices, quantities, notes, and
        condition), your trips (including locations, dates, and notes), packing lists, kits,
        photos you upload, and other content you create, so that we can provide the Service.
      </p>

      <h3>Purchase Information</h3>
      <p>
        Purchases of Packstack Pro are processed by the platform you buy through: the Apple App
        Store, Google Play, or, on the web, Stripe through RevenueCat Web Billing. We never
        receive or store your full payment card details. We use <strong>RevenueCat</strong> to
        manage purchases. RevenueCat receives purchase receipts and history, subscription status,
        and your Packstack account ID, so we can unlock Pro features on every device you use.
      </p>

      <h3>Usage and Diagnostic Information</h3>
      <p>In our apps:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Mixpanel</strong> records which features you use (for example, creating a
          packing list or sharing a trip). These events are linked to your account ID, and in the
          web app also to your email address and username.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sentry</strong> receives crash and error reports, including device or browser
          details and your account ID, email address, and username, so we can find and fix bugs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Expo</strong> receives basic, non-identifying performance and usage data from
          the mobile app, such as app version, platform, and launch counts.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>On our website (www.packstack.io):</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> collects aggregate page view and visitor data
          without cookies and without identifying you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ahrefs Web Analytics</strong> collects aggregate website traffic data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Ads</strong> conversion tracking uses cookies to measure whether visitors
          who arrive from our ads go on to sign up or download the app. See Section 3.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Mobile App Permissions</h3>
      <p>
        The mobile app asks for one permission: <strong>Photo Library (add only)</strong>, used
        only when you choose to save a trip summary image to your photos. You can change this at
        any time in your device settings.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide, operate, and maintain the Service, including syncing across your devices</li>
        <li>Create and manage your account and unlock the features you have purchased</li>
        <li>Calculate weight totals, calorie, food, and water estimates, and over-packing warnings</li>
        <li>Research trail details and product specifications to fill in your trips and gear</li>
        <li>Send sign-in codes and other emails about your account</li>
        <li>Send occasional product updates, which you can unsubscribe from at any time</li>
        <li>Understand how the Service is used, fix bugs, and build new features</li>
        <li>Measure the effectiveness of our advertising</li>
        <li>Respond to your questions and support requests</li>
        <li>Detect and prevent fraud, abuse, and security incidents</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Web app (app.packstack.io).</strong> We use cookies that are strictly necessary to
        keep you signed in. The app also stores analytics identifiers in your browser's local
        storage for Mixpanel.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Website (www.packstack.io).</strong> The Google Ads tag sets cookies so that
        Google can tell us when a visit from one of our ads leads to a sign-up or app download.
        Google may use these cookies under its own privacy policy. You can block or delete cookies
        in your browser settings, and manage ad personalization at
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">adssettings.google.com</a>. Plausible does not use
        cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>4. How We Share Information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with third parties for
        their own marketing.
      </p>

      <h3>Service Providers</h3>
      <p>We use these providers to run the Service. They process data only to provide their services to us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>DigitalOcean</strong>: hosting, database, and file storage for the apps</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong>: hosting for our website</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong>: email delivery</li>
        <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> and <strong>Stripe</strong>: purchases and billing</li>
        <li><strong>Apple</strong> and <strong>Google</strong>: sign-in, app distribution, and in-app purchases</li>
        <li><strong>Mixpanel</strong>, <strong>Sentry</strong>, and <strong>Expo</strong>: product analytics, error reporting, and app diagnostics</li>
        <li><strong>Plausible</strong>, <strong>Ahrefs</strong>, and <strong>Google Ads</strong>: website analytics and ad measurement</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Anthropic</strong> and <strong>Serper</strong>: to research trail details (such as
          distance, elevation, and typical temperatures) and product specifications, we send trail
          and location names, the month of your trip, and gear brand and product names. We do not
          send your name, email address, or hiker profile.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Content You Make Public</h3>
      <p>
        When you share a trip, anyone with its link can view the trip and its packing lists,
        without an account. Trips you publish may also appear in public listings on our website
        and be indexed by search engines. Your public profile (username, display name, bio, profile
        photo, and social links) can be viewed by anyone. Think about what you include before you
        share.
      </p>

      <h3>AI Assistants You Connect</h3>
      <p>
        If you connect an AI assistant such as Claude or ChatGPT to your Packstack account, we
        share the data you authorize, such as your gear closet, trips, and packing lists, with that
        assistant at your direction. What the assistant's provider does with that data is governed
        by its own privacy policy. You can disconnect an assistant at any time in Settings under
        Connected apps.
      </p>

      <h3>Legal Requirements and Business Transfers</h3>
      <p>
        We may disclose information if required by law or in response to valid legal process, such
        as a court order or subpoena. If Packstack is involved in a merger, acquisition, or sale of
        assets, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data Storage and Security</h2>
      <p>
        Your data is stored on servers hosted by DigitalOcean in the United States. We use
        industry-standard measures to protect it, including encryption in transit (TLS) and access
        controls. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee
        absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your information for as long as your account is active. When you delete your
        account, we delete your account and its content from our systems right away. Copies in our
        backups are removed as those backups expire. Our service providers keep analytics and error
        data for their standard retention periods. We may keep some information longer where the
        law requires it, such as purchase records.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete information</li>
        <li>Delete your account and associated data</li>
        <li>Object to or restrict certain processing of your data</li>
        <li>Receive a portable copy of your data</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can edit most of your information directly in the Service, and export your gear closet
        as a CSV file. For anything else, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Deleting Your Account</h3>
      <p>
        You can delete your account and all of its data yourself at any time: in the mobile app,
        open the menu and go to Account Details, then Permanently Delete Account; on the web, go to
        Settings, then Delete account. You can also email
        <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a> and we will delete it within
        30 days. Deleting your account does not cancel a subscription bought through the App Store
        or Google Play; cancel those in your store account settings.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children under 13. If we learn that we have, we will delete it promptly.
        If you believe a child under 13 has given us personal information, please contact us at
        <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. California Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) gives you the
        right to know what personal information we collect, to request its deletion or correction,
        and to opt out of its sale or sharing for cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not
        sell personal information. Our website's Google Ads conversion tracking may be considered
        "sharing" under the CCPA; you can opt out by blocking or deleting cookies in your browser,
        or by contacting us. To exercise your rights, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>10. International Users</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the Service from outside the United States, your information is transferred to,
        stored, and processed in the United States, which may have different data protection laws
        than your country.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we will
        update the Effective Date above and, where appropriate, notify you in the Service. Your
        continued use of the Service after a change means you accept the updated policy.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:</p>
      <p>
        Packstack, LLC<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:support@packstack.io">support@packstack.io</a>
      </p>
    </main>

    <PageFooter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
